+// FORGE_SPD_CHECKERS_KL (default 0 = lock code; needs FORGE_SPD_KING_LINES): make_move() takes the new checkers
+// from the mover's king lines when they are already built (the search has asked is_legal / gives_check for the
+// move) and the move is an ordinary move of a piece other than the king: the moved piece checks iff its target
+// is a check square of its type, and no other piece can check unless the mover was a sole blocker of one of its
+// own sliders and left that line. King moves (castling included), en passant, promotions, such discovering
+// moves and positions without king lines keep the lock's attackers_to(). With king moves left out, the result
+// equals attackers_to() for every pseudo-legal move, legal or not, of a position whose side not to move is not
+// in check. The engine reaches no other position: set_fen() refuses one, only legal moves are made, and the
+// null move is not made in check. 2 = as 1, and attackers_to() is still computed and must agree (test builds
+// only).
+#ifndef FORGE_SPD_CHECKERS_KL
+#define FORGE_SPD_CHECKERS_KL 0
+#endif
+
 bool Board::make_move(const Move& move, Undo& undo) {
     const Color us = side_;
     const Color them = opposite(us);
@@ -1065,7 +1079,22 @@ bool Board::make_move(const Move& move, Undo& undo) {
